# Build-context exclusions. NOTE: this file was introduced with BR_20260730,
# when the Dockerfiles started `COPY skills /app/skills` (the R9.1 declared tree)
# instead of a single doctrine.md. COPY brings the tree in VERBATIM — including
# things git never tracked — so the exclusions git already enforces must be
# restated here or they leak into published images.
#
# Deliberately minimal: only artifacts that are regenerable, private, or unusable
# inside a container. Anything the server reads at runtime MUST NOT be listed.

# skills/bodesign/.gitignore marks these the maintainer's product-board vault:
# "NEVER distribute: these point at the maintainer's product board data
# (customer/product names)". They are dangling symlinks in a checkout, so a COPY
# would ship broken links pointing at host paths that do not exist in the image.
# skill_shipping.py also excludes them from every archive it builds; this is the
# same rule applied one layer down, at the image boundary.
skills/bodesign/openmv
skills/bodesign/thesmart_products

# Sibling-skill pointers that only resolve in a ~/.claude/skills INSTALL layout
# (engines/emc -> ../../emc). They dangle in a plain checkout and would dangle in
# the image too. The container resolves these engines via BODESIGN_EMC_SKILL /
# BODESIGN_*_SKILL under /opt/bodesign-engines instead, so shipping broken links
# adds only noise. skill_shipping excludes them from archives for the same reason.
skills/bodesign/engines/emc
skills/bodesign/engines/datasheets

# Regenerable byte-code / per-run analysis artifacts (mirrors the same skill
# .gitignore, and the exclusions skill_shipping._EXCLUDED_DIRS applies).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/analysis

# Local runtime + VCS state: never part of an image.
.git
.run
.logs
.venv
.pytest_cache
.artifacts
.work
packages/eda-bridge/elk/node_modules
